Enduring Global and American Issues", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1160, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "06:30PM", "timeEnd": "09:00PM", "startDt": "06/14/2021", "endDt": "07/30/2021", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 5, "netid": "ds90", "firstName": "David", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Silbey"}], "pattern": "T", "facilityDescr": "To Be Assigned", "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": "TBA", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=3288"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "DC", "locationDescr": "Washington, DC", "startDt": "06/14/2021", "endDt": "07/30/2021", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "HY", "instrModeDescrshort": "HY-OLIP", "instrModeDescr": "Hybrid-Online and In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "AMST", "catalogNbr": "3071", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "SP2", "sessionBeginDt": "05/31/2021", "sessionEndDt": "08/21/2021", "sessionLong": "Summer Special Session 2", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "The US and the global community face a number of complex, interconnected and enduring issues that pose challenges for our political and policy governance institutions and society at large.\u00a0 Exploring how the US and the world conceive of the challenges and take action on them is fundamental to understanding them.\u00a0 This course investigates such issues, especially ones that fit into the critically important areas of sustainability, social justice, technology, public health and globalization, security and conflict, among others. Students will engage with these areas and issues and the challenges they pose, using multiple frameworks and approaches, through weekly class discussions and lectures.\"", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(SBA-AS, GLC-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring, Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2790, "crseId": 351417, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "3141", "titleShort": "Prisons", "titleLong": "Prisons", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1095, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "06/01/2021", "endDt": "06/17/2021", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 3, "netid": "mfk2", "firstName": "Mary", "middleName": "Fainsod", "lastName": "Katzenstein"}, {"instrAssignSeq": 4, "netid": "mcs378", "firstName": "Matthew", "middleName": "C", "lastName": "Saleh"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Online Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=1883"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "06/01/2021", "endDt": "06/17/2021", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "AD", "instrModeDescrshort": "DL-AD", "instrModeDescr": "Distance Learning-Asynchronous", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "AMST", "catalogNbr": "3141", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "3W1", "sessionBeginDt": "06/01/2021", "sessionEndDt": "06/17/2021", "sessionLong": "Three Week - First", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "The United States stands alone among Western, industrialized countries with its persistent, high rates of incarceration, long sentences, and continued use of the death penalty. This \"American exceptionalism\" -- the turn to mass incarceration -- has been fostered by the use of sharply-delineated categories that define vast numbers of people as outlaws and others as law-abiding. These categories that are based on ideas of personal responsibility and\u00a0assumptions about race are modified somewhat by a liberal commitment to human rights.\u00a0\u00a0 Our purpose in this course is to understand how such ideas have taken root and to locate the consequences of these ideas for policy and practice.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(SBA-AS, SSC-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Winter, Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "cata